{{Quote|People of Onderon, the time has come to take back our freedom. We have all been deceived. King Rash is a traitor who has sold Onderon to the Separatists for the crown. But Onderon is ours.|Steela Gerrera|<ref name="Soft War">{{TCW|The Soft War}}</ref>}}
'''Steela Gerrera''' was a [[Gender|female]] [[Onderonian]] [[human]] who lived on the [[planet]] [[Onderon]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. She fought with the [[Onderon rebels]], and was their leader, taking the position from her older brother [[Saw Gerrera]]. The efforts of her movement, with assistance from the [[Jedi]], saw the end of [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] rule through their proxy, [[Sanjay Rash|King Sanjay Rash]], on Onderon and the restoration of the benevolent [[Ramsis Dendup|King Ramsis Dendup]]. She was romantically involved with the Onderon-born politician [[Lux Bonteri]]. Gerrera was killed in the [[Onderonian Civil War|final battle]] against Onderon's droid garrison and was mourned as a hero of her people.

==Biography==
===The Clone Wars===
====Battle of Onderon====
When the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] took control of [[Onderon]], Steela Gerrera, her brother [[Saw Gerrera|Saw]], and other insurgents then fled into Onderon's wilderness. There, she and the other insurgents organized themselves into a [[Onderon rebels|resistance force]]. After her brother and former Separatist [[Senator]] [[Lux Bonteri]] contacted the [[Jedi High Council|Jedi Council]],<ref name="A War on Two Fronts" /> she then met the council's envoy, [[Jedi]] [[Jedi Master|Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], [[Jedi Knight|Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]], his [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]], and [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]].<ref name="Bio gallery">{{Databank|steela-gerrera-biography-gallery|Steela Gerrera Biography Gallery}}</ref>

[[File:IzizRebelSafehouse-FR.png|thumb|left|250px|Steela and the other rebel leaders regrouped inside Iziz]]
Gerrera then brought them to their camp, where she, Bonteri, her brother and the other insurgents were trained. At first Gerrera did not like the idea of off-worlders being involved in Onderon's affairs. However, she knew that was how [[Ramsis Dendup]] was deposed of by [[Sanjay Rash]].<ref name="Bio gallery" /> During their training, Gerrera proved herself as a talented [[Sniper|sharpshooter]]. After eliminating a detachment of the [[Separatist Droid Army|droid army]], Gerrera and the others planned to infiltrate the [[capital]] of [[Iziz]] by posing as [[Hunting|hunters]] and foragers. She and the others then split up to gather supplies and meet during the night.<ref name="A War on Two Fronts" />

[[File:Onderon_Rebels_rescue.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Steela leads the rescue of King Dendup]]
Gerrera knew they needed to win the people's trust. Thus, Gerrera planned an attack on the [[Onderon power generator|power generators]]. She, her brother and Bonteri then took out a [[droid]] patrol that then summoned a [[Armored Assault Tank Mk I|AAT]]. Together, they took the [[tank]] to the generators and destroyed them. Gerrera was then elected leader of the resistance, much to the chagrin of her brother.<ref name="Front Runners">{{TCW|Front Runners}}</ref> Steela then sent out a broadcast to the people, speaking out against Rash and the Separatist occupation forces. When news came that Rash planned on [[Death|executing]] Dendup, Gerrera knew they did not have the resources to rescue him right away. She planned on rescuing him during his execution, but her brother was then captured by [[General]] [[Kalani]]'s guards. During the execution, Gerrera and the others were able to stop the execution, but were then surrounded by [[battle droid]]s. However, her brother was able to convince [[Royal Onderon Militia|Royal Militia]]<ref name="Soft War" /> General [[Akenathen Tandin]]<ref name="TCW CE">''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars: Character Encyclopedia - Join the Battle!]]''</ref> and his men to help them escape and free Onderon.<ref name="Soft War" /> Gerrera, her resistance, and the Royal Militia then fled to the [[Onderon highlands|Highlands]].<ref name="Tipping Points" />

====Death====
[[File:Steela_dies_on_Onderon.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Steela tragically passed at the revolution's climax]]
Steela, Ahsoka, and Lux arrived just in time to save the king from the droids. On the nearby battle field, Saw shot down the last of the enemy [[HMP droid gunship|gunships]], but the damaged unit careened out of control, right into the rebel camp. Steela was trapped on a collapsing rock on the edge of a cliffside, broken loose by the droid's impact, and while trying to jump to safety, she was caught hanging from the cliff. Lux rushed to save her, but nearly fell off himself. Ahsoka used the Force to float him to safety, but as she tried to do the same for Steela, the downed gunship fired a laser blast through Ahsoka's left shoulder, breaking her concentration and causing Steela to inadvertently fall to her death.<ref name="Tipping Points" />

===Legacy===
{{Quote|Is that your sister?"<br />"Steela. This is all I have left of her.|Saw Gerrera, to Ezra Bridger|<ref name="Ghosts of Geonosis">{{Rebels|Ghosts of Geonosis}}</ref>}}
[[File:Steela_garerra_rebels.png|thumb|right|275px|A holographic image of Steela was all Saw had left of his sister even twenty years after her death.]]
Following Steela's death, Saw became disillusioned with the Jedi.<ref name="Rebel Rising" /> He carried a [[hologram]] projector of his sister to remind him of her. When Saw's militia was confronted by [[Clone Force 99]] following the [[Proclamation of the New Order]], Saw lamented, stating that the Empire would undermine all that was fought for, as well as all those who were lost, such as Steela, during the Clone Wars.<ref name="TBBAftermath">{{TBB|Aftermath (episode)}}</ref>

Saw later told the story of Steela's death to [[Jyn Erso]] during her childhood while she was under his care. When arguing with one of his allies, [[Idryssa Barruck]], Saw said that Barruck reminded him of Steela, and said his comment was not entirely a compliment.<ref name="Rebel Rising">''[[Rebel Rising]]''</ref>

During an [[Mission to investigate Geonosis|investigation]] on [[Geonosis]], Saw managed to drop the projector of her but it was recovered by [[Ezra Bridger]] who asked if the woman in the hologram was Saw's sister, him saying that the image was all he had left of her.<ref name="Ghosts of Geonosis" />

As [[Wilmon Paak]] finished connecting a [[rhydonium fuel pipe siphon]] to allow the [[Partisans]] to steal fuel, Saw basked in the smell of the [[poison]]ous vapor, alarming Paak. Saw referred to the [[rhydonium]] as his sister, insisting that it loved him.<ref name="I Have Friends Everywhere">{{Andor|I Have Friends Everywhere}}</ref> During the [[Destruction of Jedha City]] and after parting ways with his ward [[Jyn Erso]], whom he saw as his own daughter and only remaining family,<ref name="R1Novel">[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (novelization)|''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story'' novelization]]</ref> Saw called out to Steela in his last seconds of life after his Partisans' [[Catacombs of Cadera|base]] on [[Jedha]] was destroyed by the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Rogue One 3">[[Rogue One Adaptation 3|''Rogue One Adaptation'' 3]]</ref>

==Personality and traits==
Steela Gerrera was an [[Onderonian]] [[human]]<ref name="A War on Two Fronts" /> [[Gender|female]]<ref name="Databank" /> who was 1.79 [[meter]]s (5 [[Foot|feet]], 10 inches) tall,<ref name="Join the Battle" /> with [[Color|black]] [[hair]], teal [[eye]]s, and dark skin. Steela was a freedom fighter and member of the Onderon Resistance. She saw herself as more of a soldier than a leader, leaving the fiery speeches to her brother.<ref name="A War on Two Fronts" /> However, she came to realize she was a far better leader than Saw<ref name="Join the Battle" /> and assumed command of the rebels in her own way.<ref name="Front Runners" />

==Skills and abilities==
Steela was an expert shot with a vast range of blasters<ref name="Join the Battle" /> and was known for her sharpshooting skills.<ref name="A War on Two Fronts" /> She was talented in both armed and unarmed combat and was an excellent leader.<ref name="Join the Battle" /> Steela's reconnaissance and infiltration skills enabled her to plan out and lead successful scouting missions and later attack on Onderon's power generators in the capital city of Iziz.<ref name="Front Runners" />

==Equipment==
Steela used multiple weapons, including an [[A140 blaster pistol]] and a [[sniper rifle]].<ref name="A War on Two Fronts" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|I will say this about Steela. When I think of her, I think that she's one of the biggest regrets I have this season, which is I wish we hadn't killed her. We all ended up liking that character very much. I thought she was very successful. Dawn-Lyen Gardner played her and played her brilliantly. I just thought that there was an opportunity to bring a character like that back in the future because we liked her so much by the time we were ready to kill her. But in the writers' room, we didn't feel like we could tell that story and let everybody get off scot-free. It just couldn't work out that neat and there had to be a price paid for their freedom, and it ended up being Steela for various reasons.|Dave Filoni|<ref name="Filoni interview">{{SW|url=news/interview-dave-filoni-on-star-wars-the-clone-wars-season-five-part-1|text=Interview: Dave Filoni on ''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' Season Five, Part 1}}</ref>}}
Steela Gerrera was created for the Onderon arc of the [[The Clone Wars: Season Five|fifth season]] of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' animated series<ref name="Filoni interview" /> and first appeared in "[[A War on Two Fronts]],"<ref name="A War on Two Fronts" /> which premiered on [[October 6]], [[2012]].<ref name="A War on Two Fronts EG old">{{SW|url=explore/the-clone-wars/ep502|text="A War on Two Fronts" - ''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide|nolive=1}}</ref> She was voiced by [[Dawn-Lyen Gardner]].<ref name="Steela interview">{{SW|url=news/interview-dawn-lyen-gardner-steela-gerrera-on-the-clone-wars|text=Interview: Dawn-Lyen Gardner &mdash; Steela Gerrera on ''The Clone Wars''}}</ref> She was created by ''[[Star Wars]]'' creator [[George Lucas]] as a sister to Saw Gerrera,<ref name="Filoni interview" /> who he had previously created for the unproduced live-action television series ''[[Star Wars: Underworld]]''<ref name="New-R1">{{StarWarsShow|Filn82qphCA|New Rogue One Characters Revealed, LEGO Star Wars: The Freemaker Adventures|sw_url=video/the-star-wars-show-episode-7}}</ref> and that he now wanted to involve in ''The Clone Wars''. The people behind the series also wanted a brother/sister duo on Onderon and Steela would also act as a natural foil to Ahsoka Tano concerning Lux Bonteri. Series supervising director [[Dave Filoni]] later said in an interview that killing off Steela Gerrera was one of his biggest regrets he had for the season as they all had come to like the character and her portrayal and he would have liked the opportunity to bring her back later, but the writers felt that it was important to have one of the main rebel characters had to die for the story to work.<ref name="Filoni interview" /> Gardner got the role after having auditioned and only learned that it was for ''The Clone Wars'' when she got the role.<ref name="Steela interview" /> The voice actors all recorded their lines together in a group.<ref name="Kishino interview">{{SW|url=news/interview-andrew-kishino-saw-gerrera-on-the-clone-wars|text=Interview: Andrew Kishino - Saw Gerrera on ''The Clone Wars''}}</ref> Gardner and Saw Gerrera's actor [[Andrew Kishino]] had been friends already prior to working together on the series, but hadn't known that the other had been cast before meeting at the first session. Gardner used historical leaders and revolutionaries like [[Wikipedia:Martin Luther King Jr.|Martin Luther King Jr.]] as well as current revolutionary world events as inspiration for her character's journey.<ref name="Steela interview" />

Character illustration concept art of Steela Gerrera was done by [[Wayne Lo]] and a piece of concept art of Gerrera and Bonteri on a cart for "A War on Two Fronts" was drawn by [[Will Nichols]].<ref name="A War on Two Fronts EG">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/a-war-on-two-fronts-episode-guide|text="A War on Two Fronts" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref>

